# Audio is binary. NOT optional, and not covered by the repo root.
#
# The root .gitattributes sets `* text=auto eol=lf` and then exempts a list of binary
# extensions -- .png, .jpg, .pdf, .xlsx and so on. `.wav` is not on that list, so without
# this file every WAV here would fall through to `text=auto` and depend on git's
# NUL-byte heuristic to be left alone.
#
# That heuristic would almost certainly get it right. It is still the wrong thing to rely
# on, for the reason the root file spends twenty lines explaining: `core.autocrlf`
# silently rewrote every LF in tests/fixtures/testsets/retention_v1.jsonl on 2026-08-05,
# the suite broke on a checkout that changed no committed content, and no diff was visible
# because git's own autocrlf-aware diffing treated the two as equivalent. A single reflowed
# byte in a WAV moves its sha256, and manifest.json pins a sha256 per file precisely so
# that two ASR arms can be compared on identical bytes. Declared beats inferred.
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.flac binary
*.png binary

# The ground truth is matched as verbatim Thai text and its bytes are the reference every
# CER and WER is computed against. Inherit the root's LF rule explicitly rather than by
# accident.
*.txt text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
